        { 'name' => 'cue', 'kind' => 'method', 'summary' => 'Schedules a callable (C<&code>) for execution and returns an instantiated L<C<Cancellation>|/type/Cancellation> object to cancel the scheduling of the code for execution (which is especially important if you specify the C<:every ( time )> named parameter). The adverbs control when and how the code is run: run. Alternatively C<$in> is the number of seconds (possibly fractional) to wait before running the code. If C<$at> is in the past or C<$in> is negative,', 'sigs' => ['method cue(&code, Instant :$at, :$in, :$every, :$times = 1; :&catch --> Cancellation)'], 'returns' => ['Cancellation'] },
